WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.059 --> 00:00:07.610
- Health officials in China are trying to
identify a mysterious strain of pneumonia.

00:00:07.610 --> 00:00:11.290
- [Reporter] China, ordering a quarantine
for the entire city of Wuhan,

00:00:12.460 --> 00:00:16.780
where the contagious coronavirus was first
detected and is spreading fast.

00:00:18.690 --> 00:00:23.311
Detected or suspected in at least 11
countries across the globe,

00:00:23.978 --> 00:00:30.439
concerns of a global pandemic are spreading from
a virus that’s now reached the United States.

00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:34.823
- A Washington state man has died
from coronavirus, the first death

00:00:34.823 --> 00:00:36.670
from that disease here in the U.S.

00:00:36.670 --> 00:00:41.440
- [Reporter] The NBA is now urging its
players to avoid high-fiving fans.

00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:45.169
- [Reporter] Major event organizers and
cities face the difficult choice of

00:00:45.170 --> 00:00:47.019
whether to cancel big public events.

00:00:47.030 --> 00:00:51.380
- [Reporter] The NBA is telling teams they
should be prepared for the possibility

00:00:51.380 --> 00:00:53.479
of playing games in empty arenas.

00:00:53.830 --> 00:00:56.730
- [Reporter] The teams insist that
they won’t play without fans.

00:00:56.910 --> 00:00:59.686
- If I show up to an arena and ain’t
no fans in there, I ain’t playing.

00:00:59.830 --> 00:01:03.099
- I mean you just gotta be prepared
for anything, and at the same time,

00:01:03.410 --> 00:01:05.010
keep living, keep doing what we do.

00:01:05.059 --> 00:01:10.364
- NBA, MLB, NHL, MLS banning all
nonessential personnel from their

00:01:10.420 --> 00:01:11.960
locker rooms until further notice.

00:01:11.960 --> 00:01:14.720
- [Reporter] Golden State Warriors
confirming they will play

00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:16.399
without fans tomorrow night.

00:01:16.839 --> 00:01:20.039
March Madness will also be
closed to the general public.

00:01:20.369 --> 00:01:22.500
- [Reporter] Today, the World
Health Organization officially

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:23.759
calling it a pandemic.

00:01:32.313 --> 00:01:33.429
- Just a regular road trip.

00:01:34.570 --> 00:01:37.350
Rudy and I, we generally sit
across the aisle from each other.

00:01:37.910 --> 00:01:42.839
Royce, Emmanuel and Bojan behind me,
and then Mike behind Rayjon Tucker.

00:01:45.309 --> 00:01:46.427
Got there the night before.

00:01:48.229 --> 00:01:51.430
We were pretty excited for
this game, just ready to go.

00:01:55.240 --> 00:01:57.050
We knew Rudy was gonna
be out for the game.

00:01:57.050 --> 00:01:59.189
He’s, you know, feeling a little bit sick.

00:02:02.309 --> 00:02:03.130
We get to the game.

00:02:03.139 --> 00:02:03.700
We warm up.

00:02:06.039 --> 00:02:09.299
Everything is going real smooth,
and next thing you know, you see

00:02:09.300 --> 00:02:11.519
a bunch of guys in suits run out.

00:02:17.559 --> 00:02:18.660
I thought it was the FBI.

00:02:20.730 --> 00:02:24.929
- You knew something was going on as
soon as you looked out on the court.

00:02:25.530 --> 00:02:27.510
I was two rows from the court.

00:02:28.590 --> 00:02:31.660
You saw people that you usually don’t
see during that time of the game.

00:02:31.660 --> 00:02:35.079
You saw the Thunder’s assistant
general manager talking to officials.

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:39.270
Their team doctor, Donnie Strack,
who was also talking to officials.

00:02:41.109 --> 00:02:45.929
- There was so much confusion, so many
little red flags as an NBA reporter that

00:02:45.954 --> 00:02:47.929
said something is different and wrong.

00:02:52.349 --> 00:02:53.989
- I got a call from the league office.

00:02:54.489 --> 00:02:56.764
Fans were in the seats, ready to go.

00:02:57.296 --> 00:03:00.401
We were now five or 10 minutes past
the point we were supposed to tip.

00:03:06.136 --> 00:03:07.541
- I’ve been part of game delays before.

00:03:07.541 --> 00:03:09.077
There was, like, a leak
coming out of the ceiling.

00:03:09.077 --> 00:03:11.946
So it really felt like that, outside
of the guys rushing the floor.

00:03:14.918 --> 00:03:16.818
We were just told we just gotta go back.

00:03:20.784 --> 00:03:23.925
I walked back thinking, “All right,
we’ll be back out in, like, 45 minutes.”

00:03:25.965 --> 00:03:29.597
- At first we’d heard from an Oklahoma
City television reporter that law

00:03:29.597 --> 00:03:32.600
enforcement was on their way to the
arena to help evacuate, and so our first

00:03:32.600 --> 00:03:35.470
indication was, “Is this a bomb threat?”

00:03:39.107 --> 00:03:40.608
- Then we got to the locker room.

00:03:41.242 --> 00:03:44.879
We were told Rudy had it, and at that
point, we were kinda just silent.

00:03:46.848 --> 00:03:48.149
That’s when it became scary.

00:03:50.141 --> 00:03:54.489
- Due to unforeseen circumstances,
the game tonight has been postponed.

00:03:54.489 --> 00:03:56.090
You are all safe.

00:03:56.361 --> 00:03:57.859
Thank you for coming out tonight.

00:03:58.426 --> 00:03:59.527
Good night, fans.

00:04:04.365 --> 00:04:08.959
- Our Shams Charania at The Athletic
actually broke the news that

00:04:08.960 --> 00:04:10.972
Rudy Gobert had coronavirus.

00:04:11.339 --> 00:04:15.489
- In that moment, we made the decision
we should be taking a hiatus.

00:04:16.344 --> 00:04:17.378
- There was no hesitation.

00:04:17.560 --> 00:04:19.530
There was no call to
the Board of Governors.

00:04:19.781 --> 00:04:21.510
There was no consultation with anybody.

00:04:21.860 --> 00:04:23.210
Adam Silver just shut the league down.

00:04:25.219 --> 00:04:25.953
- This is crazy.

00:04:25.953 --> 00:04:26.721
This can’t be true.

00:04:26.940 --> 00:04:29.619
I mean, it’s not within
the realm of possibilities.

00:04:29.619 --> 00:04:31.959
It’s just a scene more like
out of a movie than reality.

00:04:35.290 --> 00:04:38.166
- I honestly thought we were gonna be
like, “All right, we’re going back to the hotel.”

00:04:38.599 --> 00:04:41.560
 Then come to find out the hotel
that we stayed at was under lockdown.

00:04:42.370 --> 00:04:44.339
No hotels would take us.

00:04:45.920 --> 00:04:50.510
- We’re sitting down, kind of
outside the door where the players

00:04:50.510 --> 00:04:54.380
leave, and you’re seeing health
officials come through with boxes.

00:04:56.270 --> 00:05:00.070
- When I saw them come in with their
suits and equipment and masks, the

00:05:00.070 --> 00:05:03.960
stuff we see today, you’re like, “All
right, this is, like, the real deal.”

00:05:07.495 --> 00:05:10.840
- The reporters that travel and cover
the team, we’re in direct contact

00:05:10.840 --> 00:05:12.040
with these players all the time.

00:05:12.040 --> 00:05:15.579
We’re in very close proximity,
talking right next to their faces.

00:05:20.942 --> 00:05:24.370
They got us all tested, including
the team and the traveling party, and

00:05:24.720 --> 00:05:27.080
left the arena a little after 1 a.m.

00:05:31.470 --> 00:05:32.930
- I slept about 20 minutes that whole night.

00:05:35.480 --> 00:05:38.693
8:30 the next morning, that’s
when I found out that I had it.

00:05:40.128 --> 00:05:41.696
One of the scariest
experiences of my life.

00:05:43.620 --> 00:05:47.150
My biggest concern was I had
just seen my mother and my sister

00:05:47.240 --> 00:05:48.260
four or five days before that.

00:05:48.840 --> 00:05:52.100
And I called them like, “Look, you
have to get tested right away.”

00:05:56.990 --> 00:06:00.081
I went back home, and I had to
separate myself from my family.

00:06:01.330 --> 00:06:05.570
I’m in the basement by myself, and
I have no windows in my basement.

00:06:06.560 --> 00:06:07.680
You don’t know if it’s 4 p.m.

00:06:07.680 --> 00:06:08.350
or 4 a.m.

00:06:09.340 --> 00:06:09.849
It’s Monday.

00:06:09.849 --> 00:06:10.890
Will it come on Tuesday?

00:06:10.929 --> 00:06:12.010
Tuesday, temperature’s the same.

00:06:12.040 --> 00:06:12.950
Will it come on Wednesday?

00:06:12.950 --> 00:06:14.609
Wednesday, will it come on Thursday?

00:06:15.320 --> 00:06:19.410
And I was down there
for about 10, 11 days.

00:06:22.230 --> 00:06:24.170
At the end of the day, I’m 23.

00:06:24.170 --> 00:06:27.310
You know, I’m a kid,
and I still have fears.

00:06:27.360 --> 00:06:29.950
Obviously having the virus, I feel
a certain—a different way than most.

00:06:33.549 --> 00:06:34.979
I wish people understood
a little bit more.

00:06:39.854 --> 00:06:43.850
- Once the NBA shut down, it felt like
the first domino had fallen, and it was

00:06:43.850 --> 00:06:47.650
just a matter of time for every other
domino to start falling, for the leagues

00:06:47.650 --> 00:06:49.749
to start saying, “This is not safe.”

00:06:50.520 --> 00:06:54.119
- March Madness, one of the greatest
spectacles in all of sports, has

00:06:54.119 --> 00:06:57.620
been knocked out, and the four
major professional sports leagues

00:06:57.620 --> 00:07:00.289
in North America have been silenced.

00:07:00.450 --> 00:07:03.160
For how long is anyone’s guess.

00:07:14.322 --> 00:07:18.020
- The season just began off-kilter.

00:07:19.170 --> 00:07:23.698
The tweet by the Rockets’ GM about
the protesters in Hong Kong,

00:07:25.466 --> 00:07:29.860
and then we mourn the loss of David
Stern, the former commissioner.

00:07:31.205 --> 00:07:39.013
And then on that Sunday, when we got the
news on Kobe, it was…you’re just empty.

00:07:52.270 --> 00:07:57.180
- So people were already kind of
in this emotional vortex and this

00:07:57.190 --> 00:08:01.170
emotional conflict when all of a
sudden, boom, here’s a pandemic.

00:08:04.290 --> 00:08:07.660
I don’t think the gravity hit
the players until there was the

00:08:07.660 --> 00:08:09.700
first positive test in the NBA.

00:08:10.969 --> 00:08:15.790
It was just a really grave
wakeup call about what we were

00:08:15.790 --> 00:08:17.040
about to be confronted with.

00:08:20.219 --> 00:08:25.409
And then for that to be compounded
by then having unprecedented level of

00:08:25.419 --> 00:08:32.450
racial conversations as we’re talking
about police violence and institutional

00:08:32.450 --> 00:08:34.220
racism and systemic oppression.

00:08:34.659 --> 00:08:39.740
In this situation where my humanity
is at stake, where the humanity of

00:08:39.740 --> 00:08:44.859
my people is at stake, do I want
to be the entertainment right now?

00:08:47.390 --> 00:08:51.160
I think a big reason why this entire
conversation that we’re having in this

00:08:51.160 --> 00:08:55.659
country is at the level that it is is
because there has been no sports to

00:08:55.660 --> 00:09:00.950
distract anybody, is because we have
no choice but to sit here and reflect.

00:09:01.900 --> 00:09:03.130
- We have a moment in time.

00:09:03.130 --> 00:09:05.562
People are gonna look back, our
kids are gonna look back at this

00:09:05.640 --> 00:09:07.068
and say, “You were a part of that.”

00:09:08.369 --> 00:09:12.760
I’m glad it’s something that’s sparked
a newer conversation of having athletes

00:09:12.820 --> 00:09:17.350
lead the charge, having athletes
that are not just basketball players,

00:09:17.379 --> 00:09:21.560
but that can, you know, lead and
speak on the issue intelligently.

00:09:23.270 --> 00:09:25.689
- March 11 is the night that
changed the world forever.

00:09:26.130 --> 00:09:27.610
I don’t think it’s just basketball.

00:09:28.340 --> 00:09:29.980
I think it stopped the
world in its tracks.

00:09:30.710 --> 00:09:32.280
It stopped our country in its tracks.

00:09:32.920 --> 00:09:36.400
- Your love of team and your love of sport
and the game you’ve always played is

00:09:36.459 --> 00:09:42.729
colliding with your love of family and
your love of spouse and what’s best.

00:09:44.429 --> 00:09:46.340
And there’s not an easy answer in there.

00:09:53.039 --> 00:09:57.818
I don’t know if we’re gonna see games
played the way we’ve always seen games

00:09:57.818 --> 00:10:02.390
played with 20,000 screaming fans.

00:10:14.902 --> 00:10:16.671
Is sports ever gonna be the same?

00:10:20.700 --> 00:10:25.379
If I told you I knew that
answer, I’d be lying to you.

